        <div style="background-color: #f1f3f5; padding: 12px; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">
            @* &lt;strong style="font-size: 14px; color: #333;">Definitions of technical terms used above:&lt;/strong> *@
            <strong style="font-size: 14px; color: #333;">Definitions of technical terms used on this page:</strong>
            <ul style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; padding-left: 20px; font-size: 13.5px; color: #555;">
                <li><strong>Miniratna:</strong> A special status given by the Government to high-performing public sector companies.</li>
                <li><strong>Integrated Producer:</strong> A company that handles everything from raw material mining to making the final finished product.</li>
                <li><strong>CPSE (Central Public Sector Enterprise):</strong> A company owned and run by the Central Government.</li>
                <li><strong>Mining lease:</strong> Legal permission from the government to mine a specific area.</li>
                <li><strong>Exploration:</strong> Searching and studying an area to find out how much ore it holds.</li>
                <li><strong>Beneficiation:</strong> Crushing and grinding mined ore and separating the copper-rich part from waste rock, so that the copper content rises.</li>
                <li><strong>Copper concentrate:</strong> The copper-rich material made by beneficiation. It is sent to a smelter for further processing.</li>
                <li><strong>Smelter:</strong> A plant that uses high heat to separate copper from concentrate or scrap. A primary smelter works mainly from ore concentrate. A secondary smelter works mainly from copper scrap.</li>
                <li><strong>Refinery:</strong> A plant that purifies copper to make refined copper.</li>
                <li><strong>Copper cathode:</strong> Refined, high-purity copper in sheet form.</li>
                <li><strong>LME-A grade:</strong> A high-purity grade of copper cathode accepted by the London Metal Exchange.</li>
                <li><strong>Continuous Cast Copper Wire Rod:</strong> A copper rod made by a continuous casting process. It is used to draw electrical wire.</li>
                <li><strong>Tolling:</strong> Processing material that belongs to another party, for a fee.</li>
                <li><strong>Open-pit mine:</strong> A mine dug from the surface as a large open pit, instead of underground tunnels.</li>
                <li><strong>Net sales:</strong> Total sales after deducting returns, discounts and similar items.</li>
                <li><strong>PBT (Profit Before Tax):</strong> Profit before income tax is deducted.</li>
                <li><strong>PAT (Profit After Tax):</strong> Profit left after income tax is deducted.</li>
                <li><strong>Crore:</strong> An Indian unit of counting. One crore is ten million (10,000,000).</li>
                <li><strong>Equity stake:</strong> The share of a company&rsquo;s ownership that a holder owns.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

